/// eo9:gpu-virtio — the virtio-gpu driver world (plan/09, plan/12).
///
/// `gpu.virtio` is the display sibling of `disk.virtio`/`net.virtio`: an ordinary wasm
/// component that imports the PCI capability (`eo9:pci/pci`), drives a virtio-gpu PCI
/// function's 2D control queue through configuration space, BAR registers, and DMA
/// buffers, and exports `eo9:gfx/gfx` — so a drawing program runs over a real (virtual)
/// display by composition: `gpu.virtio $ draw`.
///
/// `eo9:text/text` is imported only for one diagnostic line on first use (the probed
/// scanout geometry and completion mode); the driver works identically without a console.
///
/// There is no configure interface: the documented default behaviour is to claim the
/// first virtio-gpu function visible through the granted PCI capability on first use and
/// scan out at the host's preferred geometry (the option-C default-configuration rule,
/// plan/09 Decision 14). Selecting a specific device is `pci.filtered`'s job, composed
/// in front of the driver.
package eo9:gpu-virtio@0.1.0;

world virtio {
    import eo9:pci/pci@0.1.0;
    import eo9:text/text@0.1.0;

    export eo9:gfx/types@0.1.0;
    export eo9:gfx/gfx@0.1.0;
}
